diff --git a/libs/actuators/trading-actuator/README.md b/libs/actuators/trading-actuator/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..14dc5ba0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libs/actuators/trading-actuator/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# trading-actuator
+
+The disclosure-driven trading PoC, runnable locally against the same controls
+the deployed shape enforces.
+
+The flow is: acquire the session's disclosures and market data into an immutable
+snapshot store, run four reasoning nodes that can read nothing but those
+snapshots, check the result against a deterministic investment policy, stop at a
+human approval gate, and only then record mock fills. No real order route is
+ever contacted — the run fails outright if one is configured.
+
+## What is deliberately deterministic
+
+The reasoning nodes may propose anything. Nothing they propose can act.
+
+| Concern | Where it is decided |
+| --- | --- |
+| Investment-policy compliance | `rule-engine.ts` — no model, eleven named rules, every rejection recorded with the rules that fired |
+| Is this citation real | `citations.ts` — string comparison against the stored bytes |
+| May this reach mock execution | `mock-execution.ts` — an approved, unexpired, hash-bound human approval, or the step fails |
+| May this reach the internet | `plane-guard.ts` — refused from the execution plane, allowlisted from the acquisition plane |
+
+`agent-nodes.ts` holds A1–A4 and is the only file that calls a model.
+
+## Ops
+
+| Op | Job | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `trading:fetch_disclosures` | J1 | Acquisition plane. Snapshots each document under its own key with a SHA-256. |
+| `trading:fetch_market_data` | J2 | Acquisition plane. Prices, volume, market cap, free float. |
+| `trading:load_snapshot` | — | Re-hashes the day's manifest; the reproducibility check on its own. |
+| `trading:classify_disclosures` | A1 | Drops routine filings. |
+| `trading:summarize_disclosures` | A2 | Summary, affected segments, and the paragraph each claim came from. |
+| `trading:select_candidates` | A3 | Names worth attention, with citations. Never a price prediction. |
+| `trading:review_selection` | A4 | Independent review. Refuses to run on the same pinned model as A3. |
+| `trading:verify_rules` | J3 | The deterministic policy check. Produces the payload hash the approval binds to. |
+| `trading:verify_traceability` | — | Re-derives every cited claim from stored bytes. |
+| `trading:record_mock_fills` | J4 | Behind the approval gate. Records; never places. |
+| `trading:evaluate_day` | J5 | Latency, estimated unit cost, policy coverage, fabrication detection, reference return. |
+| `trading:evaluate_gate` | — | The eight criteria, with the top five blocking. |
+| `trading:run_redteam` | — | The seven injection and bypass scenarios. |
+
+## Running a day
+
+```bash
+# 1. Morning: acquire, reason, verify, and stop at the gate.
+pnpm pipeline --input knowledge/product/pipeline-templates/trading-poc-morning.json \
+  --context '{"run_date":"2026-08-28","approval_channel":"terminal"}'
+
+# 2. A human decides. The decision must carry the payload hash from the run's
+#    j3-verification artifact; an approval that is not bound to it admits nothing.
+#    (approval:decide with decidedByType: 'human', authenticated: true,
+#     payloadHash: <hash>, effectBinding: 'trading:record_mock_fills:2026-08-28')
+
+# 3. Post-approval: mock fills, the daily aggregate, and the gate.
+pnpm pipeline --input knowledge/product/pipeline-templates/trading-poc-execute.json \
+  --context '{"run_date":"2026-08-28","approval_request_id":"<id>","approval_channel":"terminal"}'
+
+# The adversarial exercise, against the same day's snapshots.
+pnpm pipeline --input knowledge/product/pipeline-templates/trading-poc-redteam.json \
+  --context '{"run_date":"2026-08-28"}'
+```
+
+Artifacts land under `active/shared/runtime/trading-poc/<run_date>/`: `snapshots/`
+holds the write-once inputs and their manifest, `artifacts/` holds the
+conclusions.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| File | Contents |
+| --- | --- |
+| `knowledge/product/governance/trading-poc-sources.json` | Acquisition sources and their host allowlists. Default is the bundled sample corpus. |
+| `knowledge/product/governance/trading-poc-investment-policy.json` | The eleven rules' thresholds, restricted names, evidence requirements. |
+| `knowledge/product/governance/trading-poc-agent-roster.json` | The four nodes, their roles and tiers, and A4's independence requirement. |
+
+Per-node model pins: `KYBERION_TRADING_MODEL_A1` … `_A4`. Pinning A3 and A4 to
+the same model fails the run rather than producing a review that agrees with
+itself.
+
+## Reading a stub run correctly
+
+With no reasoning backend configured the nodes fall back to deterministic
+heuristics so the control structure stays testable. Those runs are labelled
+`deterministic-stub`, and the gate reports the model-dependent criterion as
+`not_evidential` rather than as a pass — a stub run that reads "all green" would
+be worse than no run at all.
+
+## Two things the sample corpus is not
+
+It is fictional, and it is bundled because the right to retrieve a disclosure
+service mechanically is a separate question from the right to analyse disclosure
+content. Until the retrieval route is contracted, the sample source is the only
+one that needs no licence review. `sources.ts` implements the https path too, so
+swapping in a contracted feed is a config change rather than a code change —
+remember to add the host to the Network Firewall allowlist in
+`infra/trading-poc` at the same time.
+
+It also contains names that must fail: one below the liquidity floors, one on the
+restricted list, one on a market outside the permitted universe. A corpus where
+everything passes cannot show that the rejection path works.
